00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:31.550
In terms of data storage,
when we store information

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:36.710
using a geographic related index
and there are many players that

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.870
converge on one
real-world location,

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:45.290
this can create hotspots for our
reads and writes of that data.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:49.220
We have periodic events where
up to hundreds of thousands

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:53.210
of users will go to one
location or play around

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.700
the world in community
events, and this

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.910
can cause spikes of activity
for our data storage

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:02.290
and other server systems.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.630
During those times
and in general,

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:08.290
we have a high volume
of reads and writes.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:13.390
And one extra challenge is that
unlike other products where

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:18.220
users are by themselves
and any lag between users

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.480
is not visible--

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.560
even a lag of minutes may
not be apparent to the user--

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.580
in our use case, many users
are playing next to each other

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.830
and are looking at
each other's phones.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.410
So we need immediate
consistency,

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.050
because any lag of
updates between the phones

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.310
will be visible to the users.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.150
This is an example of
our need for out data

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:47.610
storage and other systems to
perform well at high volume.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:50.340
This graph is the Cloud
